William W. Austin <bill@34.mumb.atln.nrcrgais.dsl.att.net> wrote:
> 
> With the kind suggestions of George Socker <george.socker@verizon.net> I have
> solved most of my questions I posed earlier, but a new one has cropped up.  
> 
> I have a *large* collection of midi files (my wife is a musician and composer). 
> However, when I play them (alsa-0.9.0rc3) on my soundblaster using pmidi or
> playmid -a, I get monaural playback.

the output itself must be stereo.  you'll hear left/right panning.
otherwise, there might be something wrong in the mixer configuration.

if you mean the stereo "samples", then load the soundfonts with stereo
sounds.  the Creative's soundfonts include only monoraul samples.


